==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|midest|middest|middis|middst|myddest|mydest|myddis|myddst|mydst}} {{q|all obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|in middes||in the middle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/mɪdst/|[mɪdst]|[mɪtst]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-midst.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪdst|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|often|literary}} A place in the [[middle]] of something; ''may be used of a literal or metaphorical location''.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1905|author=[[w:Emma Orczy|Baroness Emmuska Orczy]]
|title=[[w:The Case of Miss Elliott|The Affair at the Novelty Theatre]]
|chapter=2|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL8479084W
|passage=Miss Phyllis Morgan, as the hapless heroine dressed in the shabbiest of clothes, appears in the '''midst''' of a gay and giddy throng; she apostrophises all and sundry there, including the villain, and has a magnificent scene which always brings down the house, and nightly adds to her histrionic laurels.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|first=Mary Ellen|last=Pitts|title=Toward a Dialogue of Understandings: Loren Eiseley and the Critique of Science|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=00JEA70gL0AC&pg=PA225&dq=%22midst%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=1H9HVK2UHOK7mQWOp4K4Dw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22midst%22&f=false|page=225|passage=At dawn, in the '''midst''' of a mist that is both literal and the unformed shifting of thought, he encounters a young fox pup playfully shaking a bone.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|first=Nathan W.|last=Schlueter|quoted_in=''One Dream Or Two?: Justice in America and in the Thought of Martin Luther King, Jr.''
|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=K-jumkcnVfEC&pg=PA8|page=89|others=1963, speech|quotee=[[w:Martin Luther King, Jr.|Martin Luther King, Jr.]]|title=[[w:I Have a Dream|I Have a Dream]]|passage=As he said in "I Have a Dream," the Negro "lives on a lonely island of poverty in the '''midst''' of a vast ocean of material prosperity."}}

